actor.description:
Selects exactly one existing actor. Must be an object, in one of two forms:
1. By id: { "actorId": "1knr9w8pjyaz6ntfubbfiwpmlacl00" }
2. By name: { "name": "counter", "key": ["demo"] }
`key` is the key parts: an array of strings, or a single string for a one-part key.
This tool never creates an actor, so `pool`, `input`, `region` and `crashPolicy` are rejected. Use rivet.actor.action or rivet.actor.request in the execute tool to create on demand.
Discover ids with the execute tool: `await rivet.actors.names.list()` then `await rivet.actors.list({ name })`.
